WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.350
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.211
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.511 --> 00:00:16.169
Unit twenty-two: Ethical Leadership. Today you will reason across time with mixed conditionals.

4
00:00:16.469 --> 00:00:19.063
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.291
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.198
Ethics.

7
00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:29.158
Ethics means moral principles that govern behaviour.

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.410
Business ethics should guide decisions, not just public relations.

9
00:00:34.017 --> 00:00:36.576
Your turn. Say: Ethics.

10
00:00:39.433 --> 00:00:40.446
Ethics.

11
00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:42.242
Integrity.

12
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.223
Integrity means consistency between one's values and actions.

13
00:00:47.817 --> 00:00:50.699
Her integrity was tested when a bribe was offered.

14
00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:53.750
Your turn. Say: Integrity.

15
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.729
Integrity.

16
00:00:58.483 --> 00:00:59.949
Transparency.

17
00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:04.540
Transparency means openness about decisions and information.

18
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:08.252
Transparency about donations built public trust.

19
00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.897
Your turn. Say: Transparency.

20
00:01:14.733 --> 00:01:15.909
Transparency.

21
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.999
Accountability.

22
00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:23.502
Accountability means readiness to accept responsibility for one's actions.

23
00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.813
Accountability means owning mistakes publicly.

24
00:01:27.417 --> 00:01:30.173
Your turn. Say: Accountability.

25
00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:34.418
Accountability.

26
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:36.301
Values.

27
00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:40.663
Values means core beliefs about what is right and important.

28
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.329
The company's values were displayed but rarely practised.

29
00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:47.964
Your turn. Say: Values.

30
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:51.952
Values.

31
00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:53.497
Dilemma.

32
00:01:54.483 --> 00:01:58.573
Dilemma means a situation requiring a choice between difficult options.

33
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:02.100
Reporting a friend's fraud posed a painful dilemma.

34
00:02:02.717 --> 00:02:05.299
Your turn. Say: Dilemma.

35
00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.111
Dilemma.

36
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:10.630
Trust.

37
00:02:11.617 --> 00:02:15.114
Trust means confidence in someone's reliability and honesty.

38
00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:18.181
Trust, once broken, is slow to rebuild.

39
00:02:18.783 --> 00:02:21.285
Your turn. Say: Trust.

40
00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.053
Trust.

41
00:02:25.817 --> 00:02:26.748
Role model.

42
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:31.096
Role model means a person whose behaviour others imitate.

43
00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:34.588
Leaders are role models whether they intend to be or not.

44
00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:37.603
Your turn. Say: Role model.

45
00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:41.944
Role model.

46
00:02:42.733 --> 00:02:46.280
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:47.117 --> 00:02:53.832
Visal, an accountant noticed irregular payments two years ago but said nothing. Now the company faces a scandal.

48
00:02:54.917 --> 00:03:02.457
It's a painful lesson. Had she spoken up earlier, the problem would not exist on this scale now.

49
00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.538
But she feared losing her job.

50
00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:17.014
Understandably. Yet if the company had a genuine speak-up culture, she would have reported it immediately. The system failed her as much as she failed it.

51
00:03:18.117 --> 00:03:20.070
What should leaders learn from this?

52
00:03:21.183 --> 00:03:31.475
That ethics must be protected structurally. If whistleblowers had been protected, the board would be dealing with a minor issue today, not a crisis.

53
00:03:32.633 --> 00:03:34.366
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:35.217 --> 00:03:37.750
Grammar focus: Mixed conditionals.

55
00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.179
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:39.883 --> 00:03:43.427
Had she spoken up earlier, the problem would not exist now.

57
00:03:44.317 --> 00:03:46.815
If he had saved money, he would be secure today.

58
00:03:47.717 --> 00:03:50.668
Had they acted sooner, we would not be in crisis now.

59
00:03:51.633 --> 00:04:03.579
Mixed conditionals link a past cause to a present result: If I had studied, I would be a doctor now. 'Had + subject + p.p.' is the formal inverted form of 'If + subject + had + p.p.'.

60
00:04:04.317 --> 00:04:08.432
Be careful! Don't say: Had she spoke up, it wouldn't exist.

61
00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:12.923
Say: Had she spoken up, it wouldn't exist.

62
00:04:13.223 --> 00:04:15.188
Had + past participle.

63
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.641
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:21.108
When Silence Is Costly.

65
00:04:21.408 --> 00:04:27.947
Ethical leadership involves not only personal integrity but also the creation of environments in which others can act ethically.

66
00:04:28.933 --> 00:04:35.670
Investigations into corporate scandals frequently reveal that employees had noticed problems long before they became public.

67
00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:43.786
Had those concerns been heard, many organisations would not be struggling with damaged reputations and legal consequences today.

68
00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:51.687
Leaders shape behaviour powerfully as role models, since employees quickly learn which values are rewarded and which are merely displayed.

69
00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:59.355
Ethical leadership is therefore demonstrated less in public statements than in how leaders respond to inconvenient truths.

70
00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:04.526
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:05.383 --> 00:05:07.766
If I had saved money, I blank rich now.

72
00:05:08.066 --> 00:05:11.615
A, would be. B, would have been. C, will be.

73
00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:17.224
The answer is A: would be.

74
00:05:18.383 --> 00:05:22.484
A situation requiring a choice between difficult options is a blank.

75
00:05:22.784 --> 00:05:26.867
A, role model. B, dilemma. C, value.

76
00:05:30.433 --> 00:05:32.433
The answer is B: dilemma.

77
00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:37.348
Readiness to accept responsibility for one's actions is blank.

78
00:05:37.648 --> 00:05:42.474
A, transparency. B, integrity. C, accountability.

79
00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:48.741
The answer is C: accountability.

80
00:05:49.883 --> 00:05:51.953
Choose the correct mixed conditional.

81
00:05:52.253 --> 00:06:01.328
A, Had she studied law, she would be a lawyer now.. B, Had she studied law, she will be a lawyer now.. C, If she studied law, she would have been now..

82
00:06:04.867 --> 00:06:08.643
The answer is A: Had she studied law, she would be a lawyer now..

83
00:06:09.783 --> 00:06:13.745
According to the reading, ethical leadership is demonstrated mainly in…

84
00:06:14.045 --> 00:06:20.032
A, public statements. B, responses to inconvenient truths. C, annual reports.

85
00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:27.250
The answer is B: responses to inconvenient truths.

86
00:06:28.433 --> 00:06:31.550
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:32.417 --> 00:06:35.531
What would you do if your manager asked you to act unethically?

88
00:06:52.317 --> 00:06:53.724
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:54.024 --> 00:07:28.182
If my manager asked me to act unethically, I would first clarify the request, because misunderstandings sometimes occur. If it were genuinely wrong, I would refuse politely but firmly, explaining my concerns and suggesting an ethical alternative. Should the pressure continue, I would raise the issue with HR or a compliance officer. Had I stayed silent, I might avoid conflict now, but I would be complicit if harm occurred later. My integrity is worth more than any single job.

90
00:07:28.482 --> 00:07:30.075
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:34.831
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and mixed conditionals.

92
00:07:35.131 --> 00:07:39.572
Today's value is integrity. Do the right thing, even when no one is watching.

93
00:07:39.872 --> 00:07:43.476
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:07:43.776 --> 00:07:46.870
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

